OL,3,GNEWSACumbria's highest inn will remain
OL,4,Apub, owner says
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe owners of Cumbria's highest inn
OL,7,Fhave said despite its closure
OL,8,Fannouncement, it will remain a pub.
OL,10,FKirkby Lonsdale Brewery, which took on
OL,11,Fthe leasehold of the centuries-old
OL,12,FKirkstone Pass Inn in April, said its
OL,13,F"memorable short chapter" had come to
OL,14,Fend, with it closing on Tuesday until
OL,15,Ffurther notice.
OL,17,FSupreme Escapes bought the site - a car
OL,18,Fpark, inn and holiday lets about
OL,19,F1,480ft (450m) above sea level - in
OL,20,F2021 after it stood empty for years.
OL,23,APub: 19-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,402,400,260,160,0,100
